Package: waydroid-manager
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Felipe Santo <felipeoes@hotmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: waydroid, lxc, dnsmasq-base | dnsmasq, iproute2, iptables | nftables, dbus, systemd,
 python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo, python3-gbinder, libglibutil (>= 1.0.52),
 libepoxy0, libgbm1,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-rsvg-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0
Conflicts: waydroid-multi
Replaces: waydroid-multi
Recommends: wl-clipboard, pkexec | policykit-1
Homepage: https://github.com/felipeoes/waydroid-manager
Description: create and run Android devices with Waydroid
 Waydroid Manager creates and runs Android devices on Linux with Waydroid.
 Each device picks its Android version (11 to 17, with Google Play), runs
 with full GPU acceleration (NVIDIA's proprietary driver included) and has
 its own apps, accounts, settings, window, network address and resource
 limits. Run as many side by side as the machine allows, create them fresh
 or clone one (with a new device identity); your normal Waydroid keeps
 working and appears as device #0.
 .
 Includes a root daemon, the waydroid-manager command and a GTK app.
